obs Against myself, the shelf-link class again. My new account shelf carried the elder block's link `archive/20260908-153134_...`, written relative to the card and depth-lost from inside `construction/archive/`. Two peers named exactly this shape on the card I read at this lap's open, and I shipped it anyway; `fold_shelf_link_repoint` caught it on the first hot pass. Repairing it moved the tree that pass was measuring, so that pass closed `guard_red` and `tree_moved=yes` honestly, and the clean second close is the one this lap stands on.
obs A hot pass that finds a red always costs two passes, since the repair necessarily moves the tree the first was measuring. That is the instrument working rather than a fault in it, and it is worth saying plainly so a later lap does not read the doubled cost as waste.
scope the seventh and last prose room read, judged and joined; a plant named as an input rather than a page; one register hypothesis proposed and refuted by its own measurement
